# Fingerprint baselines are build products, not source. They are regenerated
# wholesale by `just fingerprint <family>`, so every intentional update rewrites
# large parts of every file and the diff drowns the actual change in a PR.
#
# linguist-generated collapses them in GitHub's diff view (expandable on click)
# and drops them from the repo's language stats — without giving up the reasons
# they are text in the first place: `git diff` still works locally, `git blame`
# still works, and git can still delta-compress them.
#
# Storing them as real binary (gzip) was measured and rejected: compressed
# streams do not delta-compress, so five successive baseline updates grew the
# repo 472K as .fp.gz versus 200K as text. It would hide the diff at 2.4x the
# long-term cost, and make the baselines unreadable even locally.
#
# If you want them hidden outright rather than collapsed, change this to
# `fingerprints/** -diff` — then GitHub shows "Binary file not shown" and local
# `git diff` needs --text. That trade loses the ability to review an intentional
# baseline change, which is the whole reason the format is normalised text.
fingerprints/** linguist-generated=true

# Keep shell scripts LF on every platform; they run inside the Nix devShell.
*.sh text eol=lf
